<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@/~cl_6__para_b> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#number> "b" <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@/~cl_6__para_b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#paragraph> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@/~cl_6__para_b> <https://schema.org/text> "by inserting after subsection (1) the following subsections: \"(1A) Notwithstanding anything contained in paragraph (a) of subsection (1), and subject to any terms and conditions which may be prescribed from time to time by the Director General and on payment of the prescribed fee, the licensed registrar may permit any person— (a) who is registered as the owner of a motor vehicle, to have the registration number assigned to his motor vehicle assigned to another motor vehicle which has not previously been registered, and the licensed registrar shall thereupon assign a new registration number to the first mentioned motor vehicle; (b) who is registered as the owner of a motor vehicle, to have the registration number assigned to his motor vehicle assigned to another registered motor vehicle; or (c) who applies to be registered as the owner of a motor vehicle which has not previously been registered to have the registration number of a motor vehicle that has been cancelled for the reason that the vehicle has been broken up, destroyed or sent permanently out of Malaysia, assigned to his motor vehicle. (1B) Upon any assignment made under subsection (1A), the licensed registrar shall thereafter make all necessary consequential amendments to the register and registration certificate.\"; and"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/21/eng@> .
